<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261004164500 +0000" stop="20261004171500 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Quirky Science</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">Flight</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">Humans have long dreamed of flight—from da Vinci's flapping-wing designs to massive cow-gut-filled airships. The Wright brothers, inspired by bicycles, built strong, controllable kites that led to early planes. Modern jets fly faster thanks to high-altitude, low-resistance flight, an idea sparked by Frank Whittle's Aeolipile experiments. From the Airbus A380 to NASA's scramjet, aviation keeps evolving—what's next in flight innovation?</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire scientifique</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/3/7/9/15271973.jpg" />
