<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261004203500 +0000" stop="20261004211000 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Wonder</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">Problems</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">The Monty Hall Problem shows switching choices boosts winning odds. The Birthday Problem reveals how just 23 people can have a 50% chance of shared birthdays due to multiple pairings. Gambler's Ruin proves that in a fair game, the smaller bankroll loses over time. The Infinite Hotel Paradox explores the strange logic of infinity. The Locker Riddle uses factorization to reveal why only lockers with perfect square numbers stay open.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire scientifique</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/6/0/1/15272106.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">S1 E2</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261004211000 +0000" stop="20261004214500 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Wonder</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">Nature's Games</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">Carrion flowers like rafflesia arnoldii are rare, large, and foul-smelling, attracting flies for pollination. Aposematism uses bright colors to warn predators of toxicity, with some species mimicking these signals. Female cuckoos mimic predator calls to sneak eggs into host nests. Pheromones are chemical signals used for mating, tracking, or alarms. Deimatic behavior startles predators with sudden displays, helping prey escape.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire scientifique</category>
    <icon src="http://static-cdn.tv.sfr.net/data/img/pl/6/0/1/15272106.jpg" />
    <episode-num system="onscreen">S1 E3</episode-num>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="DocuBox.HD.fr" start="20261004214500 +0000" stop="20261004221500 +0000">
    <title lang="fr">Everyday Elements</title>
    <sub-title lang="fr">Platinum, Iodine, Aluminum, Iron, Tungsten</sub-title>
    <desc lang="fr">A series that puts chemistry in our everyday experience by showing the living connection we have with the chemicals and elements that make up our world. The matter that built skies and seas, the atoms that make up you and me, the chemistry around us that forms the things we touch, smell and see. This series shows us what the objects in our universe and in our homes are made from and why the particles around us behave as they do. Everything around us is built from Everyday Elements.</desc>
    <category lang="fr">Documentaire scientifique</category>
